 <p class="text-lg text-slate-700 italic">A 10,000mAh power bank does NOT deliver 10,000mAh to your phone. The 3.7V→5V voltage conversion costs ~35%, a "10,000mAh" unit typically delivers 6,000-6,500mAh usable. For OEM buyers, the difference between Grade-A cells (≥85% efficiency) and Grade-B cells (60-75%) is the #1 driver of customer reviews and warranty returns. This guide gives you the formula, the verification method, and the factory QC questions that separate honest specs from inflated marketing numbers.</p>
