 <section id="formula" class="mb-16">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">3. Conversion Formula: Calculating Usable Capacity for Product Spec Sheets</h2>
 <div class="bg-brandBlue rounded-2xl p-6 text-white mb-6">
 <p class="font-black text-brandOrange uppercase text-sm mb-3">THE FORMULA</p>
 <p class="text-xl font-mono mb-2"><strong>Usable mAh = (Rated mAh × 3.7V × Efficiency) ÷ Output Voltage</strong></p>
 <p class="text-slate-300 text-sm">For standard 5V USB output with 85% efficiency:</p>
 <p class="text-lg font-mono"><strong>Usable mAh = Rated mAh × 0.629</strong></p>
 </div>
 <div class="space-y-4">
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-2">Example 1: 5,000mAh Bank</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">(5,000 × 3.7 × 0.85) ÷ 5 = <strong>~3,145mAh usable</strong>, about 1 full iPhone charge</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-2">Example 2: 10,000mAh Bank</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">(10,000 × 3.7 × 0.85) ÷ 5 = <strong>~6,290mAh usable</strong>, about 1.5-2 iPhone charges</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-2">Example 3: 20,000mAh Bank</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">(20,000 × 3.7 × 0.85) ÷ 5 = <strong>~12,580mAh usable</strong>, about 3-4 iPhone charges</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>

