 <section id="mah-vs-wh" class="mb-16">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">4. mAh vs Wh: Which Unit Matters for Air Freight Compliance &amp; Labeling</h2>
 <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">Watt-hours (Wh) is the more honest unit for comparing battery capacity because it accounts for voltage differences. But for OEM importers, there is a more urgent reason to understand Wh: <strong>every lithium battery transport regulation worldwide uses Wh, not mAh</strong>. IATA, FAA, and UN38.3 all specify thresholds in watt-hours. If your factory's QC report and retail packaging only list mAh, your shipment can be rejected at origin customs.</p>

 <!-- Air Freight Compliance Table -->
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-5 border border-brandOrange/30 mb-6">
